A||N||4||DaveL||Speaker Wire Polarity||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||03-28-2000||04:30 PM||||I just replaced the dashboard speakers on my 87 SE, and I'm not entirely sure if I have them wired right. How do you tell which wire is the negative one? The wiring diagram in my Hayne's manual doesn't seem to tell me much unless some of the symbols used stand for polarity.<P>What could be the bad side of having these leads wrong?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Capt Fiero||03-28-2000||04:46 PM||||I am sorry I can not help you, but <A HREF="http://www.thefieroclub.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefieroclub.com</A>  has just made a mailing list for Fiero Audio topics and you might want to try there.  I think that is there web site.  <BR>David||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||03-28-2000||04:48 PM||||   The bad side is that you will have very little bass response and imaging will be affected.   When one speaker is wired in reverse to another speaker, the cones are always travelling in opposite directions, effectively cancelling each other out.  This effect is most noticeable in the bass frequencies.  It doesn't really matter which wire is + and which is -, as long as you wire both speakers the same.  If, for example, you have a white wire and a black wire on the left and a white wire and a black wire on the right, hook the white ones to the + terminals on your speakers and the black to the - terminals.  <P>    IF you have 4 or more speakers in your car and bass response seems to be lacking, reverse the polarity on both speakers of one pair.(both front speakers or both rear speakers)||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-28-2000||06:19 PM||||Yep, what Olympic said.||||reg||1
Z||000004||phillip||03-29-2000||08:37 AM|||| i've never tried one (i should i guess), but i think you can get one of those test and set up cd's that has speaker polarity as one of the tests. don't know if it comes in other formats though (cassette, md, etc.).||||reg||1
